CSS stands for Cascading Style Sheets.
CSS is used to design HTML tags.

There are three Ways to Insert CSS in HTML:-
    1. Inline style
    -> First Priority 
    -> We can Define Style in Tag itself.
    2. Internal style sheet
    -> Second priority
    -> We can Define Style between <style></style> 
    3. External style sheet
    -> Third priority 
    -> We can create separate file style.css 

An id and class name cannot start with a number in selector.

We can assign Colors in CSS using 3 different methods:-
    1. Color Name
    -> a valid color name like "red" , “yellow”,”gray”
    2. RGB Value
    -> an RGB value like rgb(255, 0, 0)  Value : (red,green,blue) Rang: 0 to 255
    3. Hex Value
    -> a HEX value like "#ff0000"

In table:-
tr:nth-child(odd) {background-color: #f2f2f2;}
tr:nth-child(even) {background-color: #1cc1567b;}
